a;</label><p>Value accounting for all excess apart from selection bias.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Breakdown of hazard ratio components assuming multiplicative hazards (stomach and breast cancers)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Uniform distribution</bold></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>&#x02018;Max' prop missed</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Average prop missed (&#x00025;)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>R</italic><sub>traceback</sub></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>R</italic><sub>mortality</sub></bold></th></tr><tr><th colspan="4" align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">(a) Stomach cancer</th></tr><tr><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">Hazard ratio to be accounted for <italic>R</italic><sub>DCI</sub></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">5.39</th></tr><tr><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">Due to selection bias <italic>R</italic><sub>selection</sub></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.64</th></tr><tr><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">Unaccounted for by selection bias</th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.28</th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">0.10</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">5</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1.04</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.15</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" ch